    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f99cc37_180c1df7",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/IWifiChip.hal",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 242,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-06T16:36:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as the HIDL interface is concerned, IfaceType + IfName should be unique. So, even if there is another \"wlan0\" with different type, we should be ok.\n\nBut, in the overall system. I\u0027m not sure if linux kernel can handle duplicate iface names.",
      "parentUuid": "1f99cc37_98e34d27",
